1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:03,214
The Republican Party holds the White House.

2
00:00:03,234 --> 00:00:06,501
Its 2024 platform commits to upholding the Constitution,

3
00:00:06,521 --> 00:00:10,749
defending religious liberty and empowering families.

4
00:00:10,769 --> 00:00:13,009
But a party is not judged by its promises.

5
00:00:13,029 --> 00:00:15,858
It is judged by what it does with power.

6
00:00:17,826 --> 00:00:18,182
First,

7
00:00:18,202 --> 00:00:18,505
life.

8
00:00:18,525 --> 00:00:19,972
From 1980 to 2016,

9
00:00:19,992 --> 00:00:25,148
every Republican platform backed a constitutional amendment to protect the unborn.

10
00:00:25,168 --> 00:00:25,882
In 2024,

11
00:00:26,230 --> 00:00:27,641
that pledge was gone.

12
00:00:27,661 --> 00:00:30,054
Abortion is left to the states,

13
00:00:30,074 --> 00:00:36,150
and more than a third of Republicans now say it should be legal in all or most cases.

14
00:00:37,987 --> 00:00:39,074
Marriage.

15
00:00:39,094 --> 00:00:44,677
For two decades the platform defined it as the union of one man and one woman.

16
00:00:44,697 --> 00:00:47,481
The 2024 platform no longer does.

17
00:00:47,501 --> 00:00:48,217
And in 2022,

18
00:00:48,237 --> 00:00:53,935
thirty-nine House Republicans voted to put same-sex marriage into federal law.

19
00:00:55,826 --> 00:00:57,138
The stranger.

20
00:00:57,158 --> 00:01:02,627
The President used a wartime law from 1798 to deport Venezuelans his government called gang members.

21
00:01:02,647 --> 00:01:08,908
The Supreme Court ruled that notice roughly twenty-four hours before removal “surely does not pass muster.”

22
00:01:08,928 --> 00:01:11,349
Scripture honors governing authority.

23
00:01:11,369 --> 00:01:12,678
It also commands:

24
00:01:12,698 --> 00:01:15,793
treat the stranger as the native among you.

25
00:01:17,719 --> 00:01:18,937
The poor.

26
00:01:18,957 --> 00:01:19,789
In July 2025,

27
00:01:19,809 --> 00:01:23,720
House Republicans passed their tax and spending law,

28
00:01:23,740 --> 00:01:24,785
218 to 214.

29
00:01:24,805 --> 00:01:30,382
The Congressional Budget Office estimates it adds 3.4 trillion dollars to deficits,

30
00:01:30,402 --> 00:01:33,965
and leaves ten million more people uninsured by 2034.

31
00:01:33,985 --> 00:01:38,366
Supporters call it tax relief for working families.

32
00:01:40,210 --> 00:01:40,537
Faith.

33
00:01:40,557 --> 00:01:45,225
The President created a federal task force to eradicate anti-Christian bias.

34
00:01:45,245 --> 00:01:47,456
Many believers welcome it.

35
00:01:47,476 --> 00:01:50,156
But when Christianity becomes a party’s brand,

36
00:01:50,176 --> 00:01:51,506
remember who said:

37
00:01:51,526 --> 00:01:54,014
“My kingdom is not of this world.”

38
00:01:55,864 --> 00:01:57,568
No party owns the Christian faith,

39
00:01:57,588 --> 00:01:59,602
and none stands above the truth.

40
00:01:59,622 --> 00:02:02,612
A platform shows what a party will do with power.

41
00:02:02,632 --> 00:02:04,920
When it departs from God’s design,

42
00:02:04,940 --> 00:02:07,222
whose word will we follow?
